cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use EquiMap, please cite it as below. A methods paper is in preparation; update preferred-citation once it is published."
title: "EquiMap: from SEM/EDS map tiles to phase maps, mineral identification and P-T estimates"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "van Melick"
    given-names: "Hans"
    affiliation: "Department of Earth Sciences, Utrecht University, The Netherlands"
  - family-names: "Plümper"
    given-names: "Oliver"
    affiliation: "Faculty of Geosciences and MARUM, University of Bremen, Germany"
repository-code: "https://github.com/mrln13/EquiMap"
license: GPL-3.0
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-12
keywords:
  - SEM
  - EDS
  - mosaic stitching
  - phase segmentation
  - mineral identification
  - thermodynamic modelling
  - MAGEMin
  - Perple_X
  - petrology
abstract: >-
  EquiMap is an open Python toolkit that stitches raw SEM/EDS tiles into a
  large-area mosaic that keeps its spectra, segments it into phase domains,
  suggests mineral names from a curated library, measures the length scale
  over which a bulk composition is representative, and feeds the result to
  pluggable thermodynamic backends (MAGEMin, Perple_X, pycalphad) for
  pressure-temperature estimation.
